course: dictionary
lesson: 5315
title: Keeper: a word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word keeper comes from the verb keep. A keeper is a person who looks after something or someone. «Keepers sometimes spray perfume or spices in an enclosure, because new smells give cats something to explore, like a new toy.» The clue is the animals: keepers look after the cats, so here keeper means someone who cares for animals in a zoo.
explain: Context also shows you what the keepers do. «In a zoo the food comes easily, so keepers have to give back the busy part of life, and that is called enrichment.» Keepers give animals things to do, so they are not bored. Try your meaning in the sentence: a zoo keeper fits, so you are right.
explain: Keeper can mean something different in sport. In football and hockey the keeper, or goalkeeper, stops the ball going into the goal. Always check the words near the word. If the sentence talks about a goal or a ball, keeper means the player who guards the goal. If it talks about animals or a place, it means someone who looks after it.
fact: A keeper is a person who looks after something or someone.
fact: In football and hockey, the keeper (goalkeeper) stops the ball going into the goal.
fact: In cricket, the wicketkeeper stands behind the stumps.
fact: Words ending in keeper include «zookeeper», «shopkeeper» and «beekeeper», and each one tells you what the person looks after.
fact: Keeper can also mean someone or something worth keeping, as an informal way of praising a person or thing.
exercise: «The hardest part is that a patient cannot say where it hurts, so vets rely on keepers' notes, weight, dung samples and training.» In this sentence, who are the keepers? | Children who visit the zoo | *People who look after the animals and record their health | Vets who cannot see well | People who sell tickets at the zoo
exercise: In football and hockey, what is the keeper's job? | To count the points at the end | *To stop the ball going into the goal | To run the fastest around the pitch | To score as many goals as possible
exercise: Find and copy one word from this list that ends in keeper and means someone who looks after bees. | zookeeper | goalkeeper | shopkeeper | *beekeeper
test: «At the zoo Kieran bangs on the monkey glass, and a keeper asks him to stop and he goes bright red.» What is the keeper doing? | Feeding the monkeys | Cheering Kieran on | *Asking Kieran to stop | Taking a photo of the monkeys
test: In cricket, what does the wicketkeeper stand behind? | The goal | The scoreboard | *The stumps | The net
exam: «The keeper of the keys» means: | A key that opens every door | Someone who loses the keys | Someone who makes keys for shops | *Someone who looks after the keys
